-- title:
--   Transport of 𝔪-torsion from level N₀p to level N₀
-- statement:
--   Fix a nonzero natural number $N_0$ and a prime $p$ with $p \nmid N_0$, a valuation subring $A$ of an algebraic closure $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of $\mathbb Q$ with $p$ a non-unit of $A$, a level datum $\Lambda$ of type `LevelData N₀ p A` (a morphism $\sigma_A$ from $\operatorname{Spec} A$ to $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the localisation of $\mathbb Q$ at $p$ together with a scheme $X$ over that base carrying a relative group law, a bijection $\Lambda.\mathrm{pts}$ from $J_0(N_0) = \operatorname{Pic}^0$ of the level-$N_0$ modular function field over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ onto the generic points, and a bijection $\Lambda.\mathrm{ptsSp}$ from $\operatorname{Pic}^0$ of the level-$N_0$ modular function field over the residue field $\kappa$ of $A$ onto the points over $\operatorname{Spec}\kappa$), satisfying $\Lambda.\mathrm{IsJacobian}$ (the abelian-scheme property bundle for $\Lambda.f$, commutativity of the group law, additivity and Galois-equivariance of $\Lambda.\mathrm{pts}$, additivity of $\Lambda.\mathrm{ptsSp}$, compatibility of reduction modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ with the two parametrisations whenever the reduction inputs hold, and realisability of every element of the Hecke algebra by an endomorphism of $\Lambda.f$ compatible with the group law), and an object $O$ of type `JZeroNeronObjectAtP N₀ p hpN₀ A hA Λ`, a smooth separated group scheme $O.g$ over the same base with a parametrisation $O.\mathrm{pts}$ of its generic points by $J_0(N_0p)$, compatible with addition, the Galois action and the Hecke action. Assume the Hecke inputs `HeckeInputsAll` and the commutation statements `HeckeOperatorsCommuteBar` at both levels $N_0p$ and $N_0$, so that $J_0(N_0p)$ and $J_0(N_0)$ are modules over the Hecke algebra $\mathbb T = \mathbb Z[X_\ell : \ell \text{ prime}]$. Let $\mathfrak m \subset \mathbb T$ be a maximal ideal containing the image of $p$ and not containing the generator $X_p$. Let $x \in J_0(N_0p)$ lie in $O.\mathrm{finPts}\,p$, the subgroup generated by those points killed by $p$ whose associated generic point of $O.g$ extends to a point over $\operatorname{Spec}A$, assume both degeneracy pushforwards $J_0(N_0p) \to J_0(N_0)$ for $i = 0, 1$ (pushforward along the two level-raising inclusions of function fields when the integrality and norm inputs hold, and zero otherwise) annihilate $x$, and assume $x$ is annihilated by every element of $\mathfrak m$. Let $s$ be a point of $O.g$ over $\sigma_A$ whose composite with $\operatorname{Spec} A \hookleftarrow \overline{\mathbb Q}$ is the generic point $O.\mathrm{pts}\,x$, and let $\bar s$ be its reduction, the composite of $\operatorname{Spec}\kappa \to \operatorname{Spec}A$ with $s$. Suppose that at least one of the two elements $\Lambda.\mathrm{ptsSp}^{-1}$ applied to the image of $\bar s$ under the morphism $O.\mathrm{abqFibre}\,i$ of special fibres, $i = 0, 1$, is nonzero. Then the $\mathfrak m$-torsion submodule of $J_0(N_0)$ for the level-$N_0$ Hecke action is not the zero submodule.
--
--   This is the support-transport step of Ribet's level-lowering argument in the form used here: a point of the finite part of $J_0(N_0p)[p]$ that is $\mathfrak m$-torsion, dies under both degeneracy pushforwards, and has a nonzero coordinate on one of the two abelian-quotient factors of the special fibre forces $J_0(N_0)[\mathfrak m] \neq 0$ for the same maximal ideal, under the hypothesis $U_p \notin \mathfrak m$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.JZeroNeronObjectAtP.heckeTorsion_ne_bot_of_mem_finPts_of_not_mem_toricPts`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JZeroNeronObjectAtP.heckeTorsion_ne_bot_of_mem_finPts_of_not_mem_toricPts), where the alternative to a nonzero abelian-quotient coordinate is membership in the toric part.
